<Base title="About — Paloma Cordeiro"><section class="page-hero shell"><p class="kicker">About</p><h1>Engineering with <em>ownership.</em></h1><p class="lede">I'm Paloma Cordeiro, a software engineer and tech lead based in Brazil. I build backend systems, data products and full-stack applications, and I like owning the path from architecture decision to working product.</p></section><section class="case-body shell"><aside><p class="kicker">How I work</p></aside><div><h2>Make boundaries explicit.</h2><p class="body-big">Who owns the data? What is source evidence and what is derived state? What needs history? What happens when the network, worker or user does something unexpected? Those questions shape my systems before framework choices do.</p></div></section><section class="case-body shell"><aside><p class="kicker">Capabilities</p></aside><div class="capabilities"><div><span>01</span><h3>Backend & APIs</h3><p>Python, Django, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Redis and business-domain design.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Data & ML</h3><p>ETL, Kafka, Spark, MLflow, pandas and reproducible evaluation.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Product engineering</h3><p>React, TypeScript, Astro, testing, Docker, Linux and production delivery.</p></div></div></section><section class="cta shell"><p class="kicker">Remote · Freelance · Part-time</p><h2>I’m available for projects where the hard part is understanding the system.</h2><a class="button light" href="mailto:palomacordeiro2009@hotmail.com">Get in touch ↗</a></section></Base>